"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproduced in\n- v4.5.beta1.official [46c495ca2]\n- v4.4.1.stable.fedora [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Fedora Linux 42 (Workstation Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) HD Graphics 5500 (BDW GT2) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-5600U CPU @ 2.60GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIt's a script editor bug. When editor setting _text_editor/completion/add_node_path_literals_ is on, code-completing a node path literal inside an existing one adds a redundant prefix `^` again.\n\nVideo demo:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c1b5d915-2e8f-400d-8fd3-b4a0f63f9606\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn script editor: \n1. Type: `get_node(^\".\")`\n2. Remove content inside the quotes: `get_node(^\"\")`.\n3. Place text cursor between the quotes and fire _ui_text_completion_query_ (usually [Ctrl]+[Space]).\n4. Pick any option.\n5. Get double-caret prefixed literal, e.g.: `get_node(^^\".\")`\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a (the bug is visible in a brand new project or any project with a node)\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"htt